ezy-view (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Trading safety: the volume cap no longer blocks closing positions, and
    close-all no longer gates the whole batch on the first row's quote age.
  * MT5 bridge: partial close now decrements the remaining volume across
    positions (it could close more than requested), validates side and order
    type up front, edits pending-order brackets with TRADE_ACTION_MODIFY,
    and mints the session under lock; ticket errors answer 400, not 500.
  * MT5 adapter: stop-limit orders are refused instead of silently executed
    as plain stops; trade history reads closed positions (deals showed
    qty/pnl 0); partial fills map to a new partially_filled status.
  * Paper engine: stop-out compares margin level to the maintenance rate
    (was off by 100x), limit fills use the gapped market price, SL/TP edits
    are validated, rejections are no longer persisted forever, and the
    daily-loss breaker re-arms after midnight.
  * Pine transpiler: hoisted var declarations compile, != works on series,
    and/or/not and compound assignment parse, trailing stops are enforced
    in backtests, comparisons keep per-bar history, loops step downward
    when from > to, and unsupported features now fail with clear errors.
  * Indicators: MACD/PPO/PVO signal warmup, SuperTrend flip bar and ATR
    warmup, KST scaling, RSI/RMA seed and flat-window value, StochRSI/TSI
    warmup masks, PSAR reversal step, EOM scale, VWMA zero-volume and
    linregSlope sign all match reference implementations.
  * Charts: the newest live tick is never dropped, column/high-low recolor
    on theme change, near-miss clicks grab drawings again, text/callout hit
    boxes match the renderer, the floating bar follows pan/zoom, and shared
    OHLCV/step caches no longer serve stale data.
  * UI: heatmap load errors surface instead of hanging, event source links
    are scheme-validated, template saves survive quota errors, and order
    refresh keeps modified orders in sync.
  * Dependencies: lightweight-charts 5.3, vite 8.3.8, zustand 5.1,
    lucide-react 1.76, oxlint 1.94, vitest 5.1.1, Tauri 2.12.5/2.12.6.

 -- Jack <printezy247@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000

ezy-view (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * UI kit: one primitive set for the whole app — Select, Combobox, Tabs,
    Popover, Tooltip, Dialog, Field/Checkbox/RadioGroup/Toggle/Slider/
    NumberInput/DatePicker, SegmentedControl, Badge and Toast — each with
    keyboard, focus and aria tests.
  * Every native select is gone: 18 files now use the shared listbox, so
    dropdowns share positioning, typeahead, Escape and disabled-option rules.
  * Toolbar and chart chrome rebuilt on the kit: interval pills are a
    segmented control, the box-size field is a validated number input, and
    snapshot/settings/alert/replay actions are labelled tooltip buttons.
  * Dialogs: the custom-interval and link-group dialogs moved to the shared
    Dialog shell with footer actions, describedby wiring and live validation.
  * docs/ui-audit.md records the baseline (286 raw buttons, 37 selects, 162
    inputs) and scripts/ui-audit.mjs enforces the budget from here on.

